steps.do:
If an account has fewer slots left than the customer's eligible disputes on it, tell the customer:
- the account has an open-dispute limit;
- how many open disputes it already has;
- how many more can be filed now.
Ask which to file first, then file only that many, in the customer's order. Tell them the others can be filed once an open dispute on that account is resolved, as long as each transaction is still no more than 60 days old. If no slots are left, file nothing on that account and explain why.

Confirm each filed dispute to the customer, with:
- its category;
- whether provisional credit applies: the full disputed amount, reduced by the $50 or $500 liability if reported late, issued within 10 business days of filing (20 for accounts open less than 30 days);
- the investigation timeline: 45 business days, or 90 for international transactions, POS transactions outside the US, or new accounts;
- that if the investigation finds against them, the credit is reversed, with written notice at least 3 business days before.
Name any dispute that was not filed, and say why.

Before freezing, tell the customer four things:
- all new transactions will be declined while the card is frozen;
- recurring payments will also be declined;
- pending transactions already authorized may still process;
- they can unfreeze at any time through customer service or the mobile app.

Tell the customer four things:
- the card is permanently deactivated and cannot be reactivated;
- recurring payments on it must be updated;
- refunds to the closed card will go to the linked checking account;
- for a fraud_suspected closure, they should also change their online banking password.
Ask whether they want to order a replacement card now. If yes, go to r1.

Check eligibility from f_account, r1 and v1:
- the account is OPEN, holds at least $25, and has been open at least 3 business days;
- it has no other active card and no PENDING card or order;
- the customer is at least 18 and has a US address.
An Entry tier account (Light Blue, Light Green, Green Fee-Free) must wait 48 hours after the closure. Tell the customer the earliest time they can order (the k6 closure time from f_time plus 48 hours), and do not order now.
If another requirement fails, explain what must be resolved and stop.
